  "title": "UK inflation rises to 2.9% amid energy price shocks and cost of living challenges",
  "summary": "UK inflation accelerates to 2.9% in July, driven by energy price cap resets and rising oil prices, underlining the challenge facing Andy Burnham as he seeks to shield consumers from a broader cost of living squeeze.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "UK inflation rises to 2.9% in July, driven by energy price cap resets and rising oil prices",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "July’s inflation, linked to energy costs, is expected to be the first of several in the coming months",
